    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d364">

                <pb facs="0443" n="331" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg331"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/4128: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Commission to
                        Negotiate Peace</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-03-27T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 27, 1919,
                                4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>1315. Your 1285 March 23rd, 3 am. Since American troops entered Vladivostok this
                    Government has been lending good offices to Russian Embassy in shipping Russian
                    rifles and boots, consigned to General Ivanoff-Rinoff for use of Russian forces
                    on Volga front and in Siberia. As you are aware, in our efforts to aid the
                    Czecho-Slovak armies it seemed proper to cooperate in measures to strengthen the
                    Russians who were acting with them.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
